    "pdfPageEnd": 46
  },
  "rulesText": "The spotlight is a symbol that represents the table’s attention—and therefore the immediate focus of both the narrative and the game mechanics. Any time a character or player becomes the focus of a scene, they “are in the spotlight” or “have the spotlight.”\n\nThe spotlight moves around the table organically as scenes unfold unless a mechanical trigger determines where the spotlight goes next. For example, when a player fails an action roll or rolls with Fear, the mechanics prompt the GM to seize the spotlight and make a GM move.",
  "htmlPage": {
